<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <%- include('partials/document-head') %>

    </head>
<body>
    <%- include('partials/app-header') %>

    <div class="oc-main-content">
<%- include('partials/sidebar', { currentPath: '/docs' }) %>

        <main class="oc-dashboard-area">
          <style>
            .sw-section { font-size:.7rem; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:.12em; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--oc-text-faint); padding:.6rem 0 .5rem; border-bottom:1px solid var(--oc-border); margin-bottom:.75rem; }
            .sw-section:first-of-type { margin-top:0; }
            .doc-grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(260px,1fr)); gap:.75rem; margin-bottom:1.25rem; }
            .doc-card { background:var(--oc-bg-card); border:1px solid var(--oc-border); border-radius:10px; padding:.9rem 1rem; }
            .doc-card h3 { font-size:.82rem; font-weight:700; color:var(--oc-text); margin:0 0 .4rem; display:flex; align-items:center; gap:.4rem; }
            .doc-card ul { margin:0; padding-left:1rem; list-style:disc; }
            .doc-card li { font-size:.75rem; color:var(--oc-text-muted); margin-bottom:.22rem; line-height:1.4; }
            .doc-card li strong { color:var(--oc-text-muted); }
            .doc-link { font-size:.75rem; color:var(--oc-text-muted); display:block; margin-bottom:.2rem; text-decoration:none; }
            .doc-link:hover { color:var(--oc-text); }
            .doc-note { font-size:.72rem; color:var(--oc-text-faint); font-style:italic; margin-top:.3rem; }
          </style>

          <div class="sw-section">📚 OverClaw Documentation</div>
          <p style="font-size:.8rem;color:var(--oc-text-muted);margin-bottom:1rem;">
            OverClaw is the swarm oversight dashboard  -  it reads the shared Brain / vault as its source of truth, not any single OpenClaw instance. The nav is organized around the swarm, not the runtime.
          </p>

          <div class="doc-grid">

            <div class="doc-card">
              <h3>🌐 Swarm</h3>
              <ul>
                <li><strong>Swarm Overview</strong>  -  Health of all agents at a glance: task stats, heartbeat dots, 7-day activity heatmap, alerts.</li>
                <li><strong>Project Tasks</strong>  -  Kanban for project work (Inbox → In Progress → Blocked → Done). Click a stat card on the overview to jump to that column.</li>
                <li><strong>Standing Tasks</strong>  -  Operational routines grouped Scheduled, Active, and Inactive.</li>
                <li><strong>Activity Feed</strong>  -  Live heartbeats and learnings per agent. Filter by agent pill or link from the swarm health cards.</li>
                <li><strong>Vault Graph</strong>  -  Interactive knowledge graph of the Brain / vault.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="doc-card">
              <h3>🤖 Roster</h3>
              <ul>
                <li><strong>Agents</strong>  -  High-level personas for each swarm agent: role, runtime type, machine, status. Source: vault Agent Registry.</li>
                <li><strong>Tools & Models</strong>  -  Per-agent capability cards: model family, tools available, and skill areas. The primary OpenClaw agent's model can be pulled live from the gateway config.</li>
                <li><strong>Nodes</strong>  -  Physical machines in the swarm. Shows OS, IP, assigned agents, and last heartbeat timestamp per machine.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="doc-card">
              <h3>🔁 Operations</h3>
              <ul>
                <li><strong>Dashboard</strong>  -  OverClaw home. Gateway status, version info, and quick links.</li>
                <li><strong>Scheduled Tasks</strong>  -  All loops, cron jobs, and recurring work across the swarm. OpenClaw cron jobs are pulled live; other agents' known schedules can be listed from instance config. Filter by agent.</li>
                <li><strong>Sessions</strong>  -  Active OpenClaw sessions on this instance. Shows session list, model, and recent activity.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="doc-card">
              <h3>⚙️ Settings</h3>
              <ul>
                <li><strong>Config</strong>  -  View and audit agent configuration files (SOUL.md, MEMORY.md, AGENTS.md, openclaw.json, model settings).</li>
                <li><strong>Logs</strong>  -  OpenClaw gateway application logs from this machine.</li>
                <li><strong>Debug</strong>  -  System diagnostics, API health, and troubleshooting tools for this OverClaw instance.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>

          </div>

          <div class="sw-section">🔗 External Resources</div>
          <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.3rem;margin-bottom:1rem;">
            <a href="https://docs.openclaw.ai" target="_blank" class="doc-link">📖 OpenClaw Official Docs (docs.openclaw.ai)</a>
            <a href="https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw" target="_blank" class="doc-link">🐙 OpenClaw GitHub (source)</a>
            <a href="/vault/doc?path=03%20-%20Agents/Agent%20Registry.md" class="doc-link">🗂️ Agent Registry (vault)</a>
            <a href="/vault/doc?path=03%20-%20Agents/Coordination/README.md" class="doc-link">📐 Coordination Protocol (vault)</a>
            <a href="/vault/doc?path=08%20-%20QA-and-Monitoring/README.md" class="doc-link">🏥 QA & Monitoring Guide (vault)</a>
          </div>

          <div class="sw-section">🧠 Vault Authority</div>
          <p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--oc-text-muted);line-height:1.5;">
            OverClaw reads the Brain / vault as its source of truth for agents, tasks, heartbeats, learnings, and activity. Configure the vault path in <code style="font-size:.72rem;color:var(--oc-info-text);">config/overclaw.json</code> or <code style="font-size:.72rem;color:var(--oc-info-text);">VAULT_PATH</code>.
          </p>
        </main>
    </div>

    <script>
      
    </script>
<%- include('partials/chrome-end') %>
</body>
</html>
